==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|*gloom}}, {{m|enm|*glom}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|glōm||gloaming, twilight, darkness}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*glōmaz||gleam, shimmer, sheen}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʰel-||to gleam, shimmer, glow}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|gloam|t=twilight; faint light; dull gleam}}, {{cog|no|glom||transparent membrane}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡlum/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-gloom.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|uːm|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[darkness|Darkness]], [[dimness]] or [[obscurity]].
#: ''the '''gloom''' of a forest, or of midnight''
#* '''1898''', {{w|J. Meade Falkner}}, {{w|Moonfleet}} Chapter 4
#*: Here was a surprise, and a sad one for me, for I perceived that I had slept away a day, and that the sun was setting for another night. And yet it mattered little, for night or daytime there was no light to help me in this horrible place; and though my eyes had grown accustomed to the '''gloom''', I could make out nothing to show me where to work.
# A [[melancholic]], [[depressing]] or [[despondent]] [[atmosphere]].
#* '''1855''', {{w|Robert Browning}}, [[s:Childe Roland to the Dark Tower Came|“Childe Roland to the Dark Tower Came”]], XIX:
#*: No sluggish tide congenial to the '''glooms'''; / This, as it frothed by, might have been a bath / For the fiend's glowing hoof - to see the wrath / Of its black eddy bespate with flakes and spumes.
# Cloudiness or heaviness of mind; melancholy; aspect of sorrow; low spirits; dullness.
#* Burke
#*: A sullen '''gloom''' and furious disorder prevailed by fits.
# A [[dry]]ing [[oven]] used in [[gunpowder]] [[manufacture]].

